-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Cobra
  Publisher   Ocean, 1986
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Cobra (1986)(Ocean).z80
  MD5         0268fb4d76200708849269c9747b65ff

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (-0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same file;
              probe 0xA5CD (player input, once per game update), input keyed
              to updates, game state checked at every update; beeper writes
              435 and 499 a second against the original's 437 and 500)

  Changes     1.0: figures and bullets as Next sprites; Sinclair's 48K ROM as
              the whole alt ROM, so the game starts from its own BASIC; the
              game's speed restored after every hook; the original's pace kept
              by a pace limiter and prepared sprite patterns
              1.1: rebuilt on NexClash's shared pace code; plays as 1.0 did,
              at the original's pace

  Note        Keys: any key on the loading screen and the credits, then 1 on
              the menu (5 first swaps COLOUR and MONO; COLOUR is the default).
              In play P right, O left, Q jump, A duck, M fire, N pause.
              Cobretti, the enemies, pickups, explosion pieces and bullets are
              Next sprites: white bodies, black detail, no outline, the look
              the owner approved; scenery, stars and panel keep the original's
              colours. The game plays at the original's pace, slowdowns and
              beeper timing included. It starts from the tape's own BASIC, as
              on a 48K. The archive's Infinite Lives also pokes a graphics
              pointer (34925); its one-poke version is used. Known issues: if
              Enter from the Browser is still held, the loading screen may go
              straight to the credits. Missing: no Enhanced colour set (rated
              hard: no Spec256 file, silhouette figures, scenery drawn by
              code); not yet checked: define keys, the joystick options and
              the boss of level type 2; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity
   3  Unlimited weaponry

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

